# Service registration hygiene (hard rule)

Operator incident (2026-08-15): repeated deploy runs left **multiple AIC
services registered** on the lab workstation — duplicates pointing at the same
binary, names suffixed with a lab identity, and a legacy registration from an
older product layout. The Service Control Manager waits on every registered
service at shutdown, and this is under investigation as the cause of a
multi-day shutdown hang that forced hard resets and Windows maintenance-mode
boots. The workspace already carries documented history of a `PimOfflinePim*`
doubled-prefix typo reaching a build, so name drift here is a repeat offense.

Measured on the lab host, 2026-08-15:

| Registered name | Points at | Verdict |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `aic-server-service` | `PimServer\pim-offline-server.exe` | canonical |
| `aic-offline-agent-service` | `PimAgent\pim-offline-agent.exe` | canonical |
| `aic-agent-service` | **the same** `PimAgent\pim-offline-agent.exe` | **duplicate** — second SCM wait on one binary |
| `AIC-PIM-Lab-Prop-Svc-liebsoft` | `powershell.exe` sleep loop | **name computed from an identity variable** |
| `AIC-PIM-Lab-Prop-Svc-lanicu` | `powershell.exe` sleep loop | **same defect, second copy** |
| `PIMServer` | `AIC\PIM Server\bin\pim-server.exe` | **legacy layout, off-convention name** |

`Deploy-OfflineServerDev.ps1` compounds it by probing two candidate names
(`aic-server-service`, then `aic-offline-server-service`) and using whichever
answers — tooling that accommodates drift instead of preventing it.

## The rule

> **Each product registers exactly one Windows service, under one canonical
> name declared in one authoritative place in that product's repository.
> Service names are literal constants — never composed from a timestamp, GUID,
> username, hostname, branch, version, or any other variable or build metadata.
> Installation is idempotent: creating a registration removes any prior
> registration for that product first, and a failed or interrupted install
> leaves no registration behind. No registration may point at a binary that no
> longer exists. Every deploy ends by enumerating registered services and
> proving that only the canonical set is present.**

## The canonical set

| Product | Canonical service name | Display name |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `pim-offline-server` | `aic-server-service` | AIC Server |
| `pim-offline-agent` | `aic-offline-agent-service` | AIC Agent |
| DB management agent | `aic-db-mgmt-agent-service` | AIC Database Management Agent |
| Workstation Assurance agent | `aic-workstation-assurance-agent-service` | AIC Workstation Assurance Agent |

Adding a product means adding a row here **and** to that product's install
script — in the same change set. The `%PROGRAMDATA%` / data-directory naming
contract (`OfflinePim<Agent|Server>`, never `PimOfflinePim*`) is pinned
separately by [`runtime-status.mdc`](runtime-status.mdc); service names and
data directories are two contracts and both must hold.

## Required install pattern

```powershell
# Literal constant, declared once. Never interpolated.
$ServiceName = 'aic-server-service'

# Idempotent: remove any prior registration for THIS product before creating.
foreach ($stale in @($ServiceName, 'aic-offline-server-service')) {
    if ((sc.exe query $stale 2>&1) -match 'SERVICE_NAME') {
        sc.exe stop   $stale | Out-Null
        sc.exe delete $stale | Out-Null
    }
}

try {
    sc.exe create $ServiceName binPath= "`"$exe`" --windows-scm-dispatcher" `
        DisplayName= 'AIC Server' start= auto
    if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) { throw "sc.exe create failed: $LASTEXITCODE" }
} catch {
    # An interrupted install must not leave a half-registration behind.
    sc.exe delete $ServiceName 2>&1 | Out-Null
    throw
}
```

The legacy-name list in the removal loop is the migration path: known former
names are deleted, never probed-and-adopted.

## Required end-of-deploy verification

Every deploy script ends with this, and an agent claiming a deploy succeeded
states the result:

```powershell
$canonical = @('aic-server-service','aic-offline-agent-service',
               'aic-db-mgmt-agent-service','aic-workstation-assurance-agent-service')
$found = Get-Service | Where-Object { $_.Name -match '^aic|^AIC-PIM|^PIMServer' }
$extra = $found | Where-Object { $canonical -notcontains $_.Name }
if ($extra) { Write-Error "non-canonical AIC services registered: $($extra.Name -join ', ')" }

foreach ($svc in $found) {
    $img = (Get-ItemProperty "HKLM:\SYSTEM\CurrentControlSet\Services\$($svc.Name)").ImagePath
    if ($img -match '^"([^"]+)"' -or $img -match '^(\S+)') {
        if (-not (Test-Path -LiteralPath $matches[1])) {
            Write-Error "orphaned service $($svc.Name) -> missing $($matches[1])"
        }
    }
}
```

Removing a stale registration touches machine state, so it obeys
[`host-session-safety.mdc`](host-session-safety.mdc): an install script may
delete registrations **for its own product**; an agent doing ad-hoc cleanup of
unrelated services reports the finding and asks first.

## Forbidden constructs

- More than one registered service per product, including a duplicate under a
  former name pointing at the same binary.
- `sc.exe create "AIC-Svc-$user"` / `"...-$(Get-Date -f yyyyMMdd)"` /
  `"...-$([guid]::NewGuid())"` — any name built from a variable, timestamp,
  GUID, identity, branch, or version.
- `New-Service` / `sc.exe create` without first removing the prior registration
  for that product.
- An install path that can throw after `sc.exe create` without deleting the
  registration it just made.
- A registration whose `ImagePath` binary does not exist on disk.
- Deploy tooling that **probes** candidate service names and adopts whichever
  answers, instead of asserting the canonical name.
- Declaring the service name in more than one place (script, WiX, docs) with no
  single authority — the copies drift, and the doubled-prefix typo is what that
  looks like when it ships.
- Reporting a deploy as successful without the end-of-deploy verification above.

## Worked violation to fix

**Violation** (the measured lab state). A lab helper registers a per-identity
propagation service as `"AIC-PIM-Lab-Prop-Svc-$Identity"`. Run once for
`liebsoft` and once for `lanicu`, it leaves two registrations, both hosting a
`powershell.exe` sleep loop, neither cleaned up. Separately, an agent renaming
the agent service creates `aic-offline-agent-service` without deleting
`aic-agent-service`, leaving two registrations for one binary. SCM now waits on
four extra services at shutdown, and the host hangs.

**Fix.** One literal name — `aic-lab-propagation-service` — with the identity
passed as a service **argument**, not baked into the name. The installer deletes
any prior registration (including every known former name) before creating, and
deletes on failure. The end-of-deploy check then reports the non-canonical
`aic-agent-service`, `AIC-PIM-Lab-Prop-Svc-*`, and `PIMServer` registrations by
name so they are removed deliberately rather than accumulating silently.

