## Origin

2026-08-15 — **prevents incident 3.** Repeated deploys accumulated
`aic-agent-service` alongside `aic-offline-agent-service` (same binary), two
identity-suffixed `AIC-PIM-Lab-Prop-Svc-*` registrations, and a legacy
`PIMServer`, all of which SCM waits on at shutdown — the suspected cause of the
multi-day shutdown hang and forced hard resets. Idempotent install plus the
end-of-deploy enumeration would have caught each of the four the first time it
appeared, and the literal-name requirement would have prevented the two
identity-suffixed ones from ever being created.
